{
  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "The two completed experiments (config_010, config_007) establish that multimodal + multiprofile + pca_n2000 + resnet50 + transformer yields ~0.57-0.58 accuracy, with concat fusion slightly ahead on accuracy (0.5793 vs 0.5729). The largest untested design axis is the image encoder: upgrading from ResNet50 (~25M params) to ImageNet-pretrained ViT-L (~300M+ params) could substantially improve the visual representation and thus overall accuracy. config_004 is the direct, minimal-change extension of our best result (config_007) — same RNA encoder, aggregation, profile setting, and concat fusion — swapping only the image encoder. This isolates the effect of a stronger visual backbone and reduces uncertainty about whether the current accuracy ceiling is driven by limited image representation. Expected relative cost: ViT-L is roughly 1.5–2× more expensive than ResNet50, so I estimate ~9–11 GPU hours (vs ~6.7 for ResNet50 configs). This is a justified cost increase given the potential for a meaningful accuracy jump, and with 7 experiments remaining, confirming or refuting the value of a stronger image encoder is the highest-information experiment to run next."
}

